<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rigs down 1 at 166 in week.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rigs down 1 at 166 in week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 166 rigs under contract in the U.S. Gulf as of April 11, down one from the period ending April 4, Offshore Data Services said Friday.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 179, was 92.7 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in the European/Mediterranean area remained unchanged at 103 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 104, a utilization rate of 99.0 pct.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count was up one at 573 out of a total fleet of 604, making the utilization rate 94.9 percent.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
